/-!
# The Ext sheaves of a Koszul-regular quotient into the structure sheaf, on all of `Y`

Let `Y` be a ringed space and `J ⊆ O_Y` a sheaf of ideals which, near every point of the support
of `O_Y/J`, is generated by a sequence of length `r` of sections whose Koszul complex is acyclic
in positive degrees. Then for every complex `L` presenting `O_Y/J` and every K-injective complex
`I` presenting `O_Y`, the cohomology sheaves of `𝓗om^•(L, I)` vanish in every degree `n ≠ r`.

This is the vanishing half of [Stacks, Tag 0BQZ] for a sheaf of ideals presented with constant
length; the length is the rank of the conormal sheaf, so it is locally constant, and constancy
is what a statement placing the whole object in one degree needs. The proof checks the vanishing
on an open cover: over a Koszul presentation the Ext sheaves are computed by the Koszul complex,
and off the support of the quotient the quotient restricts to zero.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.KoszulCoverIndex`: the presentations of length `r`
  and the opens off the support, indexing the cover.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.isZero_over_homology_sheafHomComplex_of_presentation`
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.isZero_over_homology_sheafHomComplex_of_one_mem`
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.isZero_homology_sheafHomComplex_of_ne`
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite TopologicalSpace
open AlgebraicGeometry HomologicalComplex

